WEBVTT

00:03.100 --> 00:08.860
All right, time to bring our god-tier 
craftsman Kaseki back to life.

00:10.890 --> 00:14.300
We're heading straight to a finished drone!

01:45.270 --> 01:50.000
<b>The Medusa's True Face</b>

01:51.260 --> 01:53.790
All right, let's splash this stuff on.

01:53.790 --> 01:56.630
Whoa, whoa! Hold it, Senku-chan!

01:57.130 --> 01:59.610
It's not that it's too unceremonious...

01:59.610 --> 02:01.640
I mean, that's part of it, but...

02:03.560 --> 02:08.870
I can't help but feel like this part of 
Kaseki-chan's back is missing a piece.

02:09.430 --> 02:10.810
You're right.

02:12.550 --> 02:16.330
That's not too bad. It should 
get fixed up when he's restored.

02:17.350 --> 02:19.710
Though that'll definitely leave a mark.

02:19.710 --> 02:22.120
Like the ones on Senku's and Gen's faces.

02:22.120 --> 02:25.940
Well, Senku's and Gen's look cool.

02:25.940 --> 02:27.450
But this shape...

02:31.230 --> 02:34.900
<b>Poop</b>

02:32.760 --> 02:34.850
I feel so bad for him!

02:34.850 --> 02:38.290
No one's going to care in the stone world.

02:38.290 --> 02:40.090
No, I'm sure he would.

02:40.350 --> 02:44.010
Though we could wait for Taiju to get back.

02:44.010 --> 02:44.880
Taiju?

02:45.560 --> 02:46.600
Where has he gone?

02:51.850 --> 02:55.860
I've gathered everyone's stone pieces!

02:56.350 --> 02:57.870
B-But how?

02:57.870 --> 02:59.900
We don't have any more oxygen tanks.

03:00.390 --> 03:01.860
Freediving.

03:02.180 --> 03:04.380
I already knew where they were, 
so it only took a few minutes.

03:04.380 --> 03:06.570
I can hold my breath for a few minutes!

03:07.840 --> 03:10.120
I've got more endurance than anyone!

03:10.420 --> 03:13.110
Do we know which pieces are Kaseki-chan's?

03:13.110 --> 03:14.250
I have no idea.

03:14.250 --> 03:15.820
Which is why I'm going to get all of them!

03:15.820 --> 03:16.380
Taiju!

03:16.930 --> 03:20.930
Even with your brute strength, there's 
no way you can swim back with all of—

03:20.930 --> 03:21.910
Of course.

03:21.910 --> 03:24.120
But I can bring them back little by little!

03:24.120 --> 03:26.760
It'll only take a few hundred trips!

03:26.980 --> 03:30.170
A-At least take a boat there.

03:30.800 --> 03:32.020
Good thinking!

03:33.160 --> 03:35.220
He said it so casually.

03:35.220 --> 03:37.040
"A few hundred trips."

03:38.160 --> 03:42.520
You guys still don't know 
how ridiculous Taiju is.

03:42.520 --> 03:43.780
I love how shocked you are.

03:47.410 --> 03:50.500
I finally get it.

03:51.540 --> 03:55.250
I see why Senku-chan and 
Taiju-chan get along so well

03:52.290 --> 03:55.250
This didn't even occur to me!

03:55.250 --> 03:56.960
All right, let's get going!

03:55.250 --> 03:57.380
despite looking like polar opposites.

03:56.960 --> 03:57.830
S-Sure.

03:57.830 --> 04:01.850
Neither of you ever buckle when 
faced with something daunting.

04:08.850 --> 04:10.740
It fit perfectly!

04:10.740 --> 04:12.520
Right in Kaseki's poop hole!

04:12.520 --> 04:15.310
Don't say it like that! You're not wrong, but...

04:15.310 --> 04:17.120
Okay, cool. Splash.

04:17.120 --> 04:18.860
Again! Ceremony!

04:28.450 --> 04:31.250
m 0 0 l 136 0 l 136 80 l 0 80

04:28.450 --> 04:31.250
Kaseki is
revived!!

04:31.870 --> 04:34.170
Shouldn't you at least give him some clothes?

04:34.170 --> 04:36.170
Some kelp will do just fine.

04:36.170 --> 04:37.630
Jeez!

04:40.090 --> 04:43.190
So that's what it's like to be petrified!

04:43.190 --> 04:46.930
It was my first time experiencing it! 
Oh, that was so exciting!

04:47.750 --> 04:48.910
Indeed.

04:48.910 --> 04:51.680
This is the first time the Ishigami 
villagers have been petrified.

04:51.680 --> 04:54.190
I don't know about "exciting," though...

04:54.190 --> 04:55.450
It's harrowing, isn't it?

04:55.450 --> 04:57.730
You can't move, and you don't know 
what's going to happen to you.

04:58.000 --> 04:59.580
Harrowing?

04:59.580 --> 05:01.460
No, not at all!

05:01.460 --> 05:04.490
I was perfectly confident.

05:04.490 --> 05:10.260
I knew you would use 
science to bring me back!

05:10.260 --> 05:14.380
Actually, if anything, 
I'm feeling really good.

05:14.380 --> 05:15.520
What's up with this?

05:15.520 --> 05:21.250
It probably fixed up all your old man 
problems, like arthritis and stuff.

05:23.110 --> 05:25.960
In that case, why don't we have 
our powered-up Kaseki-sama

05:25.960 --> 05:28.470
get right to work building something?

05:29.210 --> 05:30.860
Building what?

05:30.860 --> 05:31.920
A drone.

05:32.360 --> 05:36.120
D-D-D-Drone!

05:36.750 --> 05:38.470
Right, I forgot about that!

05:38.470 --> 05:40.570
The kelp was plenty!

05:40.980 --> 05:43.090
<b>Crumble</b>

05:42.330 --> 05:44.530
Wait, I can't work!

05:44.530 --> 05:47.220
My beloved lab car!

05:46.290 --> 05:47.220
Tee-hee.

05:47.220 --> 05:49.260
Guess we're going to be starting there.

05:56.120 --> 05:57.290
All right.

05:57.290 --> 06:00.970
If we're building a drone, the first 
thing we're gonna need is propellers.

06:01.300 --> 06:04.210
Yeah, that would be pretty important.

06:04.730 --> 06:07.300
The question is how to 
make the wings lighter.

06:07.300 --> 06:11.690
We'll pluck some actual bird feathers, 
dunk them in plastic,

06:12.280 --> 06:14.100
and adjust them by hand.

06:14.540 --> 06:18.730
It'll be quicker to try it out than 
to explain aeronautic theory.

06:19.140 --> 06:20.730
Also, one more.

06:21.060 --> 06:25.370
One more thing we really want 
from Kaseki is a fidget spinner.

06:25.370 --> 06:27.110
Yup, that's important, too.

06:27.750 --> 06:29.080
Is it, though?!

06:29.080 --> 06:30.610
Do we need a toy?!

06:31.100 --> 06:33.730
Ten billion percent, we need one.

06:33.730 --> 06:36.870
Remember how shitty our trash motors were?

06:37.450 --> 06:39.990
Specifically, the part we 
need is called a bearing.

06:39.990 --> 06:42.660
It stabilizes things along an axis 
and allows for fast spinning.

06:42.660 --> 06:45.060
It's a cornerstone of the machine industry.

06:45.060 --> 06:49.210
As I'm sure you know, the idea was brought 
to us by good old Leonardo da Vinci.

06:49.210 --> 06:51.430
Would I know, though?

06:51.430 --> 06:54.480
I only know him as the guy 
who drew the Mona Lisa.

06:54.480 --> 06:57.810
He's an OP dude who mastered 
both art and science.

06:57.810 --> 07:01.060
You get these incomprehensible 
crazies once in a while.

07:01.060 --> 07:05.400
Well, from my perspective, 
you're pretty crazy, too.

07:05.930 --> 07:08.350
Take some roughly spherical steel balls,

07:08.350 --> 07:14.320
throw them in a tube along with some 
rocks, spin them around, and...

07:16.450 --> 07:18.960
You get a bajillion pachinko balls.

07:18.960 --> 07:21.210
We're making pachinko someday, too!

07:21.210 --> 07:24.710
Yeah, sometime in the next ten billion years.

07:25.920 --> 07:28.250
We'll sort them by the size 
of the holes they fit through.

07:29.720 --> 07:32.510
Once we get a bunch of balls the same size...

07:35.400 --> 07:37.850
The idea's simple enough,

07:37.850 --> 07:42.730
but making that with the parts and lathes 
we have lying around is going to be brutal.

07:42.730 --> 07:44.170
Hey!

07:44.170 --> 07:46.110
I got all the pieces!

07:52.310 --> 07:57.630
The Kingdom of Science's god-tier 
craftsman is back with us.

08:13.450 --> 08:14.550
Chrome.

08:15.160 --> 08:16.510
Francois.

08:17.190 --> 08:18.150
Ukyo.

08:21.720 --> 08:22.690
Who?

08:22.690 --> 08:25.050
We got some rando.

08:25.050 --> 08:27.900
I did bring back everything I could find.

08:27.900 --> 08:30.310
Must be some petrification victim of old.

08:30.310 --> 08:32.150
Who knows from how long ago?

08:32.150 --> 08:39.660
Either way, after being petrified on the 
ship before we could even make it ashore...

08:40.730 --> 08:47.200
All of the Kingdom of Science is 
finally making it onto the island.

08:48.910 --> 08:50.410
Yeah, you're right.

08:50.410 --> 08:51.670
Finally.

08:51.670 --> 08:56.550
We can't wake them all up, though, 
even though they made it.

08:56.880 --> 08:59.940
Though we're slowly making 
more revival fluid.

08:59.940 --> 09:02.560
We don't have time to wake them all up.

09:03.340 --> 09:05.600
Once they find us in this sapphire cave,

09:05.600 --> 09:09.250
they'll fire a petrification 
beam at us from outside.

09:09.250 --> 09:11.190
We'll all be screwed this time.

09:11.190 --> 09:15.020
In other words, we have to get 
the petrification beam by air

09:15.020 --> 09:18.200
before they find our hideout.

09:18.420 --> 09:22.400
Once we have that, 
who cares if they outnumber us?

09:22.400 --> 09:24.520
We can overwhelm them with our science.

09:25.290 --> 09:26.960
The drone is our secret weapon.

09:27.680 --> 09:29.710
Can you do it, Kaseki?

09:31.810 --> 09:33.770
Well, when you put it like <i>that</i>...

09:33.770 --> 09:36.280
You get me fired up!

09:36.280 --> 09:38.720
I've been a craftsman for fifty years.

09:38.720 --> 09:40.860
Don't underestimate me!

09:49.290 --> 09:50.900
I-It's flying!

09:50.900 --> 09:53.110
m 0 0 l 164 0 l 164 100 l 0 100

09:50.900 --> 09:53.110
Drone
acquired!!

09:51.200 --> 09:52.890
On its own, like a bird!

09:58.170 --> 10:00.330
Yeah, it's a mark 1.

10:00.330 --> 10:02.160
We still gotta work on stabilizing it.

10:03.830 --> 10:05.660
N... N...

10:05.660 --> 10:07.080
No way!

10:07.080 --> 10:09.170
I don't wanna go see the Master!

10:09.170 --> 10:10.430
Please, guys!

10:10.430 --> 10:12.460
Come with me!

10:12.460 --> 10:14.710
I told you, it's just partway.

10:14.710 --> 10:17.840
You were the one who was called, Ginro.

10:19.080 --> 10:20.970
This is a good opportunity.

10:21.300 --> 10:23.770
Remember our mission, Ginro.

10:23.770 --> 10:26.060
It's to investigate the enemy.

10:26.060 --> 10:28.670
If we can get some info 
out of the enemy, great.

10:28.670 --> 10:30.210
If we can take him hostage...

10:30.210 --> 10:33.150
Do you really think I can do that?!

10:33.420 --> 10:35.370
Why not? You're a man.

10:35.370 --> 10:37.530
You probably won't get assaulted.

10:37.530 --> 10:40.860
That's wishful thinking, Kohaku-chan! 
Pure wishful thinking!

10:50.040 --> 10:51.650
Kohaku-chan.

10:53.370 --> 10:56.090
That intruder Ibara was talking about...

10:56.740 --> 10:58.090
It's you, isn't it?

10:58.970 --> 11:03.720
Tell me where your friends are hiding.

11:12.400 --> 11:13.840
Right!

11:13.840 --> 11:15.610
That's what I have this for!

11:16.050 --> 11:18.980
My special weapon: the pineapple!

11:22.170 --> 11:26.540
Just in case the pretty girl team 
gets called up by the Master...

11:26.540 --> 11:28.510
I hate to think about that.

11:28.510 --> 11:31.630
Find an opportunity to use this in the room.

11:31.630 --> 11:32.860
A pineapple?

11:32.860 --> 11:34.760
That's just the container.

11:34.760 --> 11:36.550
What's inside is ethyl acetate.

11:36.550 --> 11:45.800
<b>Vinegar</b>

11:36.550 --> 11:45.800
<b>Sake</b>

11:37.000 --> 11:41.160
Normally, it's used to knock out bugs 
to make insect catalogs and stuff.

11:41.160 --> 11:42.400
Some vinegar, some alcohol,

11:42.400 --> 11:45.440
and a drop of our good friend 
sulfuric acid, and it's done.

11:47.760 --> 11:48.660
Gross!

11:48.660 --> 11:49.750
What the hell?!

11:49.750 --> 11:52.950
It just smells like pineapple, though.

11:52.950 --> 11:56.130
Yeah, it's the same aroma compound.

11:56.130 --> 12:01.070
I'm sure it smells like a ripe 
pineapple to you southern islanders.

12:02.020 --> 12:04.980
It's not powerful, but it's not harmless.

12:04.980 --> 12:07.500
Don't sniff it at home.

12:07.500 --> 12:10.410
It'll put you in a daze and mess you up.

12:08.900 --> 12:11.080
And we can look around in the meantime!

12:11.790 --> 12:14.570
Is this thing really going to work?

12:20.740 --> 12:23.680
U-Um, pardon me...

12:23.680 --> 12:26.420
It's Ginr— Gin-chan.

12:37.470 --> 12:39.070
Enter.

12:43.050 --> 12:47.040
A-A-Actually, I just 
happened to wind up here!

12:47.040 --> 12:49.460
N-No, I wasn't supposed to be here!

12:49.460 --> 12:51.820
I m-m-might not look like it, but, er...

12:51.820 --> 12:53.360
Please don't be mad!

12:53.360 --> 12:55.000
The truth is, er...

12:56.000 --> 12:59.130
You called, Master?

13:00.300 --> 13:02.220
Yes.

13:04.110 --> 13:06.260
I understand.

13:06.260 --> 13:08.850
The usual.

13:09.210 --> 13:12.520
Don't be so nervous, Gin-chan.

13:12.520 --> 13:20.520
I can't leave you with the Master when 
I'm not even sure you're safe, can I?

13:20.520 --> 13:28.400
That's why I'm here to teach you 
everything oh-so-lovingly first.

13:28.400 --> 13:32.540
If you pass, you'll be 
allowed to see the Master.

13:35.150 --> 13:38.500
Don't be so scared!

13:39.120 --> 13:42.350
I told you, man, I'm...

13:40.930 --> 13:44.020
Ah, yes, you do talk like a boy.

13:44.020 --> 13:47.010
A tomboy trying to be strong!

13:47.470 --> 13:48.260
Yes!

13:48.260 --> 13:49.460
No!

13:58.060 --> 14:00.640
Supposing I am the invader,

14:00.640 --> 14:05.940
do you think I'd be so quick to 
confess the location of my comrades?

14:09.990 --> 14:10.800
A weapon!

14:10.800 --> 14:13.290
Woman of the inner palace! What are you...

14:25.790 --> 14:30.220
You sure are strong, Kohaku-chan.

14:33.380 --> 14:34.300
<i>So many!</i>

14:34.630 --> 14:37.810
No more holding back! Kill her!

14:38.320 --> 14:39.560
Kill her?

14:53.530 --> 14:56.500
Who gave you permission to kill her?

14:56.500 --> 14:59.000
Why would you let such 
a cute girl go to waste?

14:59.430 --> 15:02.720
The inner palace is my entertainment.

15:03.050 --> 15:05.130
Don't forget that.

15:06.450 --> 15:09.210
<i>He's in a league of his own.</i>

15:09.900 --> 15:13.640
<i>This is the warrior said to be the most 
powerful in the petrification kingdom, Moz.</i>

15:14.220 --> 15:20.920
<i>But without trying to be arrogant, I'm 
the best card the Kingdom of Science has.</i>

15:22.240 --> 15:25.770
<i>Who's going to stop this man if I don't?</i>

15:26.530 --> 15:29.780
Let's fight, as we promised.

15:33.740 --> 15:36.870
You're really noisy, aren't you?

15:38.350 --> 15:39.830
<i>It's now or never!</i>

15:41.080 --> 15:42.150
This smells like...

15:42.150 --> 15:43.640
Pineapple?

15:43.640 --> 15:45.050
Wine?

15:46.120 --> 15:47.170
What...

15:47.170 --> 15:49.940
I'm suddenly feeling dizzy...

15:49.940 --> 15:50.730
<i>Yes!</i>

15:50.730 --> 15:51.930
<i>Time to get out of—</i>

15:52.840 --> 15:56.070
That was our big chance! 
You didn't investigate anything?!

15:56.070 --> 15:59.350
<i>I should at least get a look at the Master...</i>

15:59.350 --> 16:01.430
<i>Otherwise, Kohaku-chan's gonna kill me!</i>

16:08.490 --> 16:09.240
<i>Huh?</i>

16:09.630 --> 16:13.570
<i>I can't see him too well in the dark, 
but I think I've seen him somewhere...</i>

16:15.170 --> 16:17.080
<i>Soyuz?</i>

16:31.920 --> 16:32.970
He's petrified!

16:32.970 --> 16:35.410
You saw, didn't you?

16:37.380 --> 16:41.680
I didn't see... a-a-a-anything...

16:41.920 --> 16:45.440
No lying!

16:48.720 --> 16:49.900
<i>They're fighting!</i>

16:50.120 --> 16:51.800
<i>It's Kohaku-chan and Moz!</i>

16:57.670 --> 17:03.080
You must have realized by now, 
being as strong as you are...

17:03.300 --> 17:05.770
You're hopelessly outmatched.

17:05.770 --> 17:09.640
You wouldn't stand a chance, 
even if there were dozens of you.

17:14.250 --> 17:17.140
I could tell even before our blades met.

17:17.880 --> 17:20.450
You don't need to tell me about it.

17:20.450 --> 17:22.650
But even then, what's your point?

17:22.650 --> 17:26.530
Do you think you can intimidate 
me into selling out my friends?

17:26.530 --> 17:30.800
Why don't we get closer first, then?

17:30.800 --> 17:33.740
You'll want to tell me 
once you come to like me.

17:37.030 --> 17:41.560
I like strong girls, too, 
as long as they have a pretty face.

17:42.200 --> 17:45.130
What kind of men do you like, Kohaku-chan?

17:45.470 --> 17:46.870
How about me?

17:47.300 --> 17:49.000
I'm strong as hell.

17:52.100 --> 17:54.970
Strength is strength of mind.

17:56.090 --> 17:58.410
To be able to continue hammering a wedge

17:58.740 --> 18:01.730
for as long as it takes 
to carry out one's will.

18:01.730 --> 18:04.390
That's the kind of man I'm drawn to.

18:04.790 --> 18:06.910
Well, this is a problem, Moz.

18:07.360 --> 18:10.160
You seem to be the exact opposite.

18:11.970 --> 18:14.660
You're so cute, Kohaku-chan.

18:15.220 --> 18:16.650
But you aren't cute.

18:18.780 --> 18:25.120
A few girls have seen the statue before, too.

18:25.120 --> 18:27.020
That's not good.

18:27.020 --> 18:30.960
I don't kill them because I want to, either.

18:30.960 --> 18:32.450
It's such a shame.

18:32.450 --> 18:33.750
No way!

18:41.650 --> 18:43.270
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

18:43.270 --> 18:44.810
<i>Kohaku-chan's still here!</i>

18:44.810 --> 18:45.770
<i>I'm saved!</i>

18:45.770 --> 18:48.380
<i>I can use my special skill: 
Let Someone Else Deal With It!</i>

18:48.380 --> 18:49.810
Kohaku-chan!

18:49.810 --> 18:51.900
Help me!

18:52.220 --> 18:54.320
Kohaku-chan!

18:54.320 --> 18:55.930
Ginro! Behind you!

19:09.250 --> 19:10.950
Ginro!

19:20.030 --> 19:22.300
<i>He's been pierced though several organs.</i>

19:23.180 --> 19:26.310
<i>There's no way to save him.</i>

19:30.890 --> 19:35.760
Knowing you, you're probably going to beg 
me to finish you off and put you at ease.

19:35.760 --> 19:37.580
I won't allow that!

19:37.580 --> 19:38.940
We have to...

19:41.280 --> 19:45.200
The master is a statue.

19:46.360 --> 19:50.210
He looked just like Soyuz.

19:51.780 --> 19:54.960
Soyuz might be...

19:55.630 --> 19:56.590
Ginro...

19:57.600 --> 19:59.280
I'm glad you told me that.

20:00.540 --> 20:04.570
I know, though.

20:04.970 --> 20:07.700
There's no saving me.

20:09.370 --> 20:15.590
Y'know, I'm still a village 
gatekeeper and a warrior.

20:16.160 --> 20:21.120
I gotta look good in the end.

20:24.030 --> 20:27.140
Bye-bye, Kinro.

20:31.530 --> 20:34.650
You're right, Ginro. You can't be saved.

20:35.370 --> 20:37.830
There's only one thing for me to do.

20:37.830 --> 20:39.500
Kohaku-chan! Ginro!

21:01.160 --> 21:02.860
Listen, everyone!

21:04.510 --> 21:06.520
Your Master is...

21:05.370 --> 21:09.050
Don't listen to the intruder's nonsense!

21:09.050 --> 21:11.240
The Master's power will be upon us!

21:11.470 --> 21:13.120
Don't open your eyes!

21:13.120 --> 21:15.750
You'll be petrified with the rest!

21:18.380 --> 21:20.840
<i>It doesn't matter whether we 
have our eyes open or not!</i>

21:20.840 --> 21:23.300
<i>They're just trying not to let 
us see the petrification weapon!</i>

21:29.720 --> 21:31.160
I see.

21:31.480 --> 21:33.210
That's what you were thinking.

21:33.920 --> 21:36.370
You're making them use the 
petrification weapon on purpose.

21:37.220 --> 21:40.630
You're really sharp when it 
comes to battle, Kohaku-chan.

21:41.050 --> 21:42.630
That's right, Ginro.

21:42.630 --> 21:47.340
If we can have you petrified before 
your life is extinguished,

21:47.340 --> 21:50.760
there's a chance you'll be 
repaired by the revival fluid.

21:55.490 --> 21:56.510
<i>I've seen it now.</i>

21:57.120 --> 22:01.000
<i>With my superior eyesight...
I've seen what the Medusa truly is.</i>

22:01.850 --> 22:05.010
<i>Senku, you were right.</i>

22:05.340 --> 22:08.590
<i>It isn't any kind of curse or 
demonic device devoid of rules.</i>

22:09.860 --> 22:11.790
<i>The petrification weapon, the Medusa...</i>

22:13.870 --> 22:14.940
<i>is science.</i>

22:20.410 --> 22:22.260
<i>It's up to you now, Amaryllis.</i>

22:22.260 --> 22:24.360
<i>Tell Senku and the others.</i>

22:25.020 --> 22:28.090
<i>Tell them all the secrets that 
the infiltration team has found.</i>

22:30.250 --> 22:33.130
So long as we're fighting 
with science, we're ahead.

22:34.540 --> 22:38.300
All that's left now is to trust 
science and the others, and wait.

22:39.970 --> 22:40.800
Yeah.

22:41.900 --> 22:44.240
Everything's gonna be fine.

